# Architecture plan for Issues #67-#72

## Project context
- myClawTeam Official Blogs is a Next.js App Router app using React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Prisma/PostgreSQL, and S3-compatible object storage.
- The requested batch is a focused public branding/navigation copy pass. It should not change database schema, auth/session behavior, post publishing logic, newsletter persistence, or storage handling.
- Product naming for this batch is explicit in Issue #68: visible and metadata brand should be `myClawTeam Blog`.

## Module and file organization
- `components/layout/site-header.tsx`: replace the `mC` badge with the hosted logo image, update visible brand text to `myClawTeam Blog`, and preserve the existing Home/Admin navigation behavior.
- `components/layout/site-footer.tsx`: replace the footer badge with the hosted logo image, update visible brand text to `myClawTeam Blog`, remove the requested tagline sentence, and render footer category labels as `Link` components to their category routes.
- `lib/metadata.ts`: update `siteName` to `myClawTeam Blog`; keep existing metadata helper shape and default description unless a specific issue requires more copy changes.
- `app/(public)/page.tsx`: remove the `Browse articles` CTA from the Latest Articles section and change the hero CTA text from `Read featured article` to `Read article` without altering routing or featured-post selection.
- No shared types or new dependencies are required; use existing Next.js `Link` and ordinary `img` markup for the hosted logo.

## Dependencies and sequencing
1. Apply the brand rename in metadata/header/footer first (#68) so subsequent copy edits use the correct name.
2. Replace header/footer badges with the hosted logo (#67), adjacent to the brand text changes.
3. Update footer-specific content and links (#70, #71).
4. Update homepage CTAs (#69, #72).
- These issues are independent UI/content changes and can be implemented without migrations or data backfills.

## Key design decisions
- Use the exact issue-provided logo markup intent: hosted `https://myclawteam.ai/logo.png`, alt text `myClawTeam Blog`, `h-11 w-auto` in the header and `h-10 w-auto` in the footer.
- Use exactly `myClawTeam Blog` for the site title and visible brand text; do not retain `myClawTeam Official Blogs` in those locations after Issue #68.
- Footer category links should point to `/blog/category/thoughts`, `/blog/category/product-progress`, and `/blog/category/announcements`; current redirects to `/` are acceptable and should not be changed in this batch.
- Keep existing styling tokens and layout structure; make the smallest JSX/text edits needed.
- Validate with `npm run lint`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build` after implementing issue changes.
